        {
            "structure": {
                "para": [
                    {
                        "id": "47",
                        "text": "Steps 1 and 2"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "48",
                        "text": "Step 1. Describe the specific event or aspect you wish to focus on.\nStep 2. Connect specific events or aspects to your course or given theory."
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "49",
                        "text": "TIP You can vary the order of Moves 2 and 3.\nTIP Give specific examples to back up your claims.",
                        "tip": true
                    }
                ]
            },
            "notes": {
                "para": []
            },
            "content": {
                "para": [
                    [
                        {
                            "id": "50",
                            "text": " This course has also taught me the difference between ‘knowing’ how people feel and understanding how people may feel from their perspective. I have learnt that it is impossible to know exactly how someone else feels and to say that one does may distract attention away from their problem. "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "51",
                            "text": " For example, my course friends and I have found the first term back at university stressful and we frequently share our feelings about this. I am often tempted to tell them ‘I know exactly how you feel’. However, I am now more considered in my response and rephrase this to something like ‘I understand how you must be feeling’. This validates what the others have said whilst letting them know I appreciate their views. "
                        }
                    ]
                ],
                "placeHolder": "Type Move 3 here.",
                "id": "50"
            }
        },
