                        "id": "61",
                        "text": "Steps 1 and 2"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "62",
                        "text": "Step 1. Admit to problems, if appropriate.\nStep 2. Interpret the situation in the light of your given framework."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "notes": {
                "para": []
            },
            "content": {
                "para": [
                    [
                        {
                            "id": "65",
                            "text": " I have also learnt "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "66",
                            "text": " the difference between "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "64",
                            "text": " empathizing and sympathizing; "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "115",
                            "text": " this is extremely beneficial to me "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "64",
                            "text": " . "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "67",
                            "text": " I am a person that "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "64",
                            "text": " can get caught up in other people's difficulties; this is neither helpful nor supportive. "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "68",
                            "text": " Much better "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "64",
                            "text": " is to empathize and remain objective as this is both helpful and supportive and may enable the other person to progress. "
                        }
                    ]
                ],
                "placeHolder": "Type Move 4 here.",
                "id": "64"
            }
        },
        {
            "structure": {
                "para": [
                    {
                        "id": "112",
                        "text": "Move 5: Comparing past with present and future"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "113",
                        "text": "This compares your present feelings and skills with your earlier ones and looks at what changes you expect to see in the future."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "notes": {
                "para": []
            },
            "content": {
                "para": [],
                "placeHolder": "",
                "id": ""
            }
        },
        {
            "structure": {
                "para": [
                    {
                        "id": "70",
                        "text": "Steps 1, 2 and 3"
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "71",
                        "text": "Step 1. Compare your past thinking to your present thinking.\nStep 2. Consider the implications for the future.\nStep 3. Conclude your reflection with reference to the task brief and your future plans."
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "72",
                        "text": "TIP Make reference to the words of the assignment task in your conclusion.\nTIP Look to the future too—what changes in yourself or the situation do you expect to see?",
                        "tip": true
                    }
                ]
            },
            "notes": {
                "para": []
            },
            "content": {
                "para": [
                    [
                        {
                            "id": "73",
                            "text": " During the course, I have learnt that before you can understand others you must first understand yourself. "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "74",
                            "text": " Sutton and Stewart (2002: 20) argue that by gaining self-awareness our chances of becoming genuine and empathic increase. "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "73",
                            "text": " This course has provided me with an opportunity to reflect on my own thoughts and my belief system. As a result of this, "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "75",
                            "text": " I am becoming more aware "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "73",
                            "text": " of my prejudices and values and have learnt that, in order to develop an empathic understanding, "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "76",
                            "text": " I need to try "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "73",
                            "text": " to suspend these so I can give a non-judgemental and respectful response. I am much more aware of how this challenges me personally. I would find it difficult to deal with racist, sexist or prejudiced people as this opposes how I have been brought up to think. However, I now understand that other people may have been brought up with a different belief system. As a result of the course, "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "77",
                            "text": " I feel more capable of being less judgemental "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "73",
                            "text": " . "
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "78",
                            "text": " Looking inward is the biggest and perhaps most difficult element of the Counselling Skills module, but the one which has been most beneficial to my personal development. "
                        }
                    ]
                ],
                "placeHolder": "Type Move 5 here.",
                "id": "73"
            }
        },
